StudentIQ is a machine learning system that predicts student academic performance (Low/Medium/High) using 29 behavioral, academic, and demographic features. It implements a complete Scikit-learn pipeline with imputation, scaling, and one-hot encoding, compares Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and Gradient Boosting classifiers, and tunes Random Forest via GridSearchCV with 5-fold cross-validation. The best model achieves 92% accuracy. Insights are visualized through EDA plots, correlation heatmaps, confusion matrices, feature importance, and multiclass ROC curves using Matplotlib and Seaborn.
